(3071544, 429147, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>You found a very lovely scene and did an exceptional job with the composition.  Overall, the image appears to be dark, as mentioned in more than one of the comments you received.  However, I believe it is an optical illusion of sorts, as people expect the sun they see breaking through the clouds to shine on the sheep themselves instead of the countryside in the background.  If you had balanced the light for the sheep, you would have received comments about the washed out sky.  Tough lighting conditions to shoot under and I think you got as much out of this image as was possible.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, You found a very lovely scene and did an exceptional job with the composition.  Overall, the image appears to be dark, as mentioned in more than one of the comments you received.  However, I believe it is an optical illusion of sorts, as people expect the sun they see breaking through the clouds to shine on the sheep themselves instead of the countryside in the background.  If you had balanced the light for the sheep, you would have received comments about the washed out sky.  Tough lighting conditions to shoot under and I think you got as much out of this image as was possible. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-11-29 10:44:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3071576, 428113, 50695, '<td valign="top">It''s so funny to think about birds sending postcards to each other. Thanks!</td>', 'It''s so funny to think about birds sending postcards to each other. Thanks!', '2006-11-29 10:50:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3071597, 429315, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>You found a very lovely scene and did a very nice job with the composition.  The size relationship between the plant and mountain give the image a lot of depth.  Where I think this image falls a little short is in the color.  The harsh sun gives the image a washed-out look.  You might want to try bumping the gamma in levels and then decreasing the brightness.  This will strengthen the colors and contrast in the mid-range features.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, You found a very lovely scene and did a very nice job with the composition.  The size relationship between the plant and mountain give the image a lot of depth.  Where I think this image falls a little short is in the color.  The harsh sun gives the image a washed-out look.  You might want to try bumping the gamma in levels and then decreasing the brightness.  This will strengthen the colors and contrast in the mid-range features. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim ', '2006-11-29 10:54:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3072035, 429449, 60862, '<td valign="top">Well, I gave you a 6! :)  I thought it was a clever, off-the-wall take, and the sentiment is dead on target.  Of course, as a traveler, sometimes I get tired of seeing the same things everywhere.  But when you''re feeling off-kilter because of being away from home for a long time, that becomes a good thing.<br/> <br/>As far as the photo itself, I like the composition.  The bland color on the walls frames the bright green of the Starbucks signs well.</td>', 'Well, I gave you a 6! :)  I thought it was a clever, off-the-wall take, and the sentiment is dead on target.  Of course, as a traveler, sometimes I get tired of seeing the same things everywhere.  But when you''re feeling off-kilter because of being away from home for a long time, that becomes a good thing. As far as the photo itself, I like the composition.  The bland color on the walls frames the bright green of the Starbucks signs well.', '2006-11-29 13:03:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3072052, 429277, 47721, '<td valign="top">I was there and a postcard like picture of the jewel makes me want to go back.... congrats... beautiful work...<br/> <br/>Have a beer at "Fortune of war" oldest pub....   great place...</td>', 'I was there and a postcard like picture of the jewel makes me want to go back.... congrats... beautiful work... Have a beer at "Fortune of war" oldest pub....   great place...', '2006-11-29 13:10:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3072174, 429220, 51660, '<td valign="top">Great shot Ragga! I love it the colors of it and the soft effect of the ocean.<br/> <br/>It certainly looks like Antarctica, and I know cause I am close to 78 degrees South right now!<br/>Of course .. the water around here is pretty stiff at the moment and taking a shot at sunset is not an option as the sun is up 24 hours a day this time of year :-)</td>', 'Great shot Ragga! I love it the colors of it and the soft effect of the ocean. It certainly looks like Antarctica, and I know cause I am close to 78 degrees South right now!Of course .. the water around here is pretty stiff at the moment and taking a shot at sunset is not an option as the sun is up 24 hours a day this time of year :-)', '2006-11-29 13:39:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3072467, 428537, 40386, '<td valign="top">This was one of my 10s in this challenge, really thought it would reach top 5 at least.  Wonderful shot, great exposure.  Congratulations.</td>', 'This was one of my 10s in this challenge, really thought it would reach top 5 at least.  Wonderful shot, great exposure.  Congratulations.', '2006-11-29 15:04:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3072475, 427774, 40386, '<td valign="top">This was one of my 10s in this challenge, some of the night shots were superb and this was one of them, really expected it to finish higher.  Congratulations none the less.<br/></td>', 'This was one of my 10s in this challenge, some of the night shots were superb and this was one of them, really expected it to finish higher.  Congratulations none the less.', '2006-11-29 15:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
