(3730929, 429326, 71249, '<td valign="top">Crossed the bridge a few months ago, never realised it was so beautiful. Great shot with wonderful colors and perspective.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-03 01:38:51.</i></td>', 'Crossed the bridge a few months ago, never realised it was so beautiful. Great shot with wonderful colors and perspective.', '2007-06-03 02:38:22.000000', '2007-06-03 02:38:51.000000', 0),
(3846621, 428537, 73452, '<td valign="top">Oh wow!  This is an amazing shot!  I love the lines of the color spurting out.  And the city background makes it such a more dynamic photo.  Thanks for the tips left over at the "Shooting Fireworks" thread, this weekend im traveling out with my grandparents to watch fireworks from the mountains...Im going to try out a few of your tricks and tips!</td>', 'Oh wow!  This is an amazing shot!  I love the lines of the color spurting out.  And the city background makes it such a more dynamic photo.  Thanks for the tips left over at the "Shooting Fireworks" thread, this weekend im traveling out with my grandparents to watch fireworks from the mountains...Im going to try out a few of your tricks and tips!', '2007-06-28 22:39:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3876624, 427168, 5112, '<td valign="top">At first reaction, it''s not an image that screams, "Look at me!"  It''s more of an image that grows on you, maybe even one that has a personal history, one where you might have a connection to the image that the rest of us can only guess.  That''s probably too much.<br/> <br/>As for it being in the "Postcard" challenge, it doesn''t scream postcard in the stereotypical definition of postcard.  Card yes, but not postcard.  That''s probably the biggest reason why people didn''t appreciate it during the challenge.<br/> <br/>As for the image itself, the technicals seem fine, and the composition is OK also.  It''s an odd picture in a way, the gentle, light colours of the rose against the dark, broody fence, the dark dead rose crossing over in front and then behind the young rose, a picture of contrasts in a way.  I think you''re right, it probably makes a beautiful print.  What''s funny is that images that look good on the net don''t necessarily make good prints (and the other way around too).<br/> <br/>I hope this helps a tad.</td>', 'At first reaction, it''s not an image that screams, "Look at me!"  It''s more of an image that grows on you, maybe even one that has a personal history, one where you might have a connection to the image that the rest of us can only guess.  That''s probably too much. As for it being in the "Postcard" challenge, it doesn''t scream postcard in the stereotypical definition of postcard.  Card yes, but not postcard.  That''s probably the biggest reason why people didn''t appreciate it during the challenge. As for the image itself, the technicals seem fine, and the composition is OK also.  It''s an odd picture in a way, the gentle, light colours of the rose against the dark, broody fence, the dark dead rose crossing over in front and then behind the young rose, a picture of contrasts in a way.  I think you''re right, it probably makes a beautiful print.  What''s funny is that images that look good on the net don''t necessarily make good prints (and the other way around too). I hope this helps a tad.', '2007-07-06 20:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3877087, 427168, 62671, '<td valign="top">I understand your frustration with the challenge.  <br/>This is a lovely image for hanging on a wall.  I would agree with the comments that it doesn''t meet the post card challenge.  Because,  think about the purpose of a post card...  They are sent to people you left behind on your vacation that says ''wow, this place is great, wish you were here!''<br/>This doesn''t meet that expectation.  <br/> <br/>It is a sad and gloomy image that has a great background and soft lighting and colors.  The ''story'' is a sad dispair kind of a feel.  Sometimes, we need to set our own personal sentimental opinions aside and look at it from another perspective. (the beauty of dpc comments btw)   This would make for a wonderful "get well" card, or "missing you" kind of card.  Its a wonderful image that has its own purpose.</td>', 'I understand your frustration with the challenge.  This is a lovely image for hanging on a wall.  I would agree with the comments that it doesn''t meet the post card challenge.  Because,  think about the purpose of a post card...  They are sent to people you left behind on your vacation that says ''wow, this place is great, wish you were here!''This doesn''t meet that expectation.   It is a sad and gloomy image that has a great background and soft lighting and colors.  The ''story'' is a sad dispair kind of a feel.  Sometimes, we need to set our own personal sentimental opinions aside and look at it from another perspective. (the beauty of dpc comments btw)   This would make for a wonderful "get well" card, or "missing you" kind of card.  Its a wonderful image that has its own purpose.', '2007-07-06 23:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3885031, 427168, 63360, '<td valign="top">I actually think the soft focus and the dark color tones work well here to set the mood.  Don''t worry about the DNMC, bc as you know, most people only look at a photo for a few seconds when voting in a challenge. <br/> <br/>As far as the composition...it bothers me a little that the top rose (what''s left of it) is directly above the main subject.  I would prefer it to be slightly off to the left, and then you could crop the photo so that both roses were on the thirds.</td>', 'I actually think the soft focus and the dark color tones work well here to set the mood.  Don''t worry about the DNMC, bc as you know, most people only look at a photo for a few seconds when voting in a challenge.  As far as the composition...it bothers me a little that the top rose (what''s left of it) is directly above the main subject.  I would prefer it to be slightly off to the left, and then you could crop the photo so that both roses were on the thirds.', '2007-07-09 09:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
